
E01: one procedure, several directions
app(R, S, [1,2])                                          3 answers: [[]+[1,2],[1]+[2],[1,2]+[]]
app([1,2], S, T)                                          first answer: [1,2|A]-A
rev(R, [1,2,3]), first answer                             first answer: [3,2,1]
rev(R, [1,2,3]), every answer                             1 answers [[3,2,1]], then no more: the inference limit ran out

E02: order
\+ X = 1, X = 2                                           fails
X = 2, \+ X = 1                                           first answer: 2
setdiff([1,2,3,4], [2,4,6], D)                            first answer: [1,3]
non_maths_major(brown)                                    first answer: yes
non_maths_major(smith)                                    fails

E03: a goal before its procedure
later(A, B), later not yet defined                        error: existence_error(procedure,later/2)

E04: a first alternative that never ends
p(A): loop(A) first, then A = 1                           no answer: the inference limit ran out
as([a,a]): left recursion, list known                     no answer: the inference limit ran out

E06: Elcock 1982, u+v=16 and w*u=v and u+10=12
is/2, in that order                                       error: instantiation_error
is/2, reordered by hand                                   first answer: [2,14,7]
clpfd, in that order                                      first answer: [2,14,7]
when/2 pass sets, in that order                           first answer: [2,14,7]

E09: x+y=10 and x-y=4
when/2 pass sets                                          first answer: [A,B]
clpfd                                                     first answer: [A,B]
clpfd, then label                                         first answer: [7,3]
clpq                                                      first answer: [7,3]

